NAME
     timecmd - how long a command takes, and other ways to run one

SYNOPSIS
     time [-p] COMMAND [ARG...]
     timeout SECONDS COMMAND [ARG...]
     nohup COMMAND [ARG...]

DESCRIPTION
     Called as time it runs COMMAND and prints how long it took -- real,
     user and system. Called as timeout it kills the command if it is
     still running after SECONDS. Called as nohup it runs the command
     with hangups ignored, so that it survives the terminal going away.

OPTIONS
     -p   the POSIX form of the timing report

SEE ALSO
     sleep(1), ps(1)
